{"subjectId":"data-science","id":"spacy","title":"spaCy Basics","group":"Natural Language Processing","order":19,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">spaCy is an industrial-strength NLP library: one call runs tokenization, part-of-speech tagging, sentence splitting, lemmatization and named-entity recognition.</p>\n<figure class=\"code\"><figcaption>Setup</figcaption><pre><code>pip install spacy\npython -m spacy download en_core_web_sm</code></pre></figure>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-cut\"></i>Tokens</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import spacy\nnlp = spacy.load(\"en_core_web_sm\")\ndoc = nlp(\"The cost of Iphone in U.K is 699$\")\nprint([t.text for t in doc])            # ['The', 'cost', 'of', 'Iphone', 'in', 'U.K', 'is', '699', '$']</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>spaCy keeps “U.K” together and splits “699$” into the number and the currency sign — rules that a plain <code>split()</code> can't know.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-tags\"></i>Parts of speech &amp; lemmas</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import spacy\nnlp = spacy.load(\"en_core_web_sm\")\ndoc = nlp(\"The cost of Iphone in U.K is 699$\")\nprint([(t.text, t.pos_) for t in doc][:4])   # [('The', 'DET'), ('cost', 'NOUN'), ('of', 'ADP'), ('Iphone', 'PROPN')]\nprint([t.lemma_ for t in nlp(\"She was running faster\")])   # ['she', 'be', 'run', 'fast']</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Tag</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Tag</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>NOUN</code></td><td>Noun</td><td><code>VERB</code></td><td>Verb</td></tr><tr><td><code>PROPN</code></td><td>Proper noun</td><td><code>AUX</code></td><td>Auxiliary (is, was)</td></tr><tr><td><code>ADJ</code></td><td>Adjective</td><td><code>ADP</code></td><td>Preposition</td></tr><tr><td><code>DET</code></td><td>Determiner (the, a)</td><td><code>NUM</code></td><td>Number</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list-details\"></i>Sentences &amp; entities</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import spacy\nnlp = spacy.load(\"en_core_web_sm\")\ndoc = nlp(\"This is the first sentence. Please check it. Let's study now\")\nprint([s.text for s in doc.sents])     # ['This is the first sentence.', 'Please check it.', \"Let's study now\"]\nents = nlp(\"Sundar Pichai joined Google in 2004 in California.\").ents\nprint([(e.text, e.label_) for e in ents])   # [('Sundar Pichai', 'PERSON'), ('Google', 'ORG'), ('2004', 'DATE'), ('California', 'GPE')]</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-school\"></i>NLTK</h3><p>A teaching toolkit: many algorithms and corpora, you assemble the pipeline yourself.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-rocket\"></i>spaCy</h3><p>Production-ready pipelines, fast, one object (<code>doc</code>) with everything — tokens, tags, lemmas, entities.</p></div></div></section>"}